{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-65451",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We can calculate the period $T$ by computing the difference in the $x$-values between two consecutive asymptotes. Therefore,\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2}{3}\\pi -(-\\frac{2}{3}\\pi )=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi )}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3x}{4})+1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
